mode: "100644"
text: "# Packaging, retention + two worked examples\n\n## Packaging (the CTR driver) — do this before scripting\n- **Title:** specific, outcome-oriented, curiosity with a clear payoff. Not a vague teaser.\n  (\"The freelance tax setup that saved me €4,000\" > \"My tax tips\".)\n- **Thumbnail:** one idea, high contrast, readable text at mobile size, accurate to the content.\n  Remove clutter before adding anything. Generate concepts with ideogram / nano-banana, then\n  **A/B test** in Studio.\n- Rule: if you can't make the packaging compelling, the idea isn't ready. Reverse the usual order.\n\n## The cold open (first 30 seconds)\nPatterns that deliver the promise instead of throat-clearing:\n- **Promise + proof:** \"By the end you'll have a tax setup that runs itself — here's the whole thing.\"\n- **Stakes:** \"I almost owed €4,000 I didn't have. This is the system that fixed it.\"\n- **Question + tease:** \"Why do freelancers always get surprised by tax? One missing step —\"\nNo logo animation, no \"welcome back to the channel.\" Start delivering immediately.\n\n## Retention structure (the AVD driver)\n- Re-hook every 60–90s: open loops (\"the third one is the one nobody does\"), pattern interrupts,\n  B-roll, location/tone changes.\n- One topic; cut anything that doesn't serve it. Chapters help Search and let viewers commit.\n- Find the retention cliffs in Studio and rewrite those exact moments.\n\n## Diagnose with three numbers (read natively in Studio)\n| Symptom | Number | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| Few impressions→clicks | **CTR** low | Packaging: title/thumbnail; A/B test |\n| Clicks but instant drop | **30s retention** low | Hook/promise mismatch in the open |\n| Holds then sags | **AVD %** low | Pacing/length; cut padding, add re-hooks |\n| Views but no growth | **Session** low | Weak end screen / no chain to next video |\n\n## Worked example A — blunt indie-founder voice\n```\nPACKAGE  Title: \"The 30% rule that saved me €4,000 at tax time\"\n         Thumbnail: a split jar (spend / tax), bold \"30%\", no clutter.\nCOLD OPEN (0–20s): \"Almost owed four grand in tax I didn't have. My fault — I tracked income,\n         not the set-aside. Here's the whole system, takes five minutes to set up.\"\nBODY     5 segments, one per step, re-hook before each. ~9 minutes. No padding.\nCLOSE    One CTA. NEXT: end screen → \"My full freelance finance setup\" (playlist start).\n```\n\n## Worked example B — warm studio voice\n```\nPACKAGE  Title: \"The calm freelance tax setup (no spreadsheets)\"\n         Thumbnail: tidy desk, soft palette, \"Tax, sorted\" — readable at mobile size.\nCOLD OPEN (0–25s): \"If tax season makes your stomach drop — by the end of this, it won't. We use\n         one account and one rule, and the panic just… goes.\"\nBODY     gentle walkthrough, em-dashes, one small step at a time, chapters. ~11 minutes.\nCLOSE    One CTA. NEXT: series link → \"Part 2: what to set aside for retirement.\"\n```\n\nBoth: read brand-profile + voice-builder first; packaged before scripted; cold-open delivers the\npromise; explicit NEXT for session contribution; description + chapters for Search; human films/\nedits/designs the thumbnail. To cut Shorts from this long-form, see captions-and-clipping.\n"
